        "statement": "Let $\\ell\\ge3$, $q=e^{\\pi i/\\ell}$, $\\delta=q+q^{-1}>0$, $k=\\ell-2$, and let $[a]=\\sin(a\\pi/\\ell)/\\sin(\\pi/\\ell)$. For the normalized closure trace $\\tau_n$, let $J_n$ be its trace-pairing radical and put $Q_n=\\mathrm{TL}_n(\\mathbb C,\\delta)/J_n$. Then $J_n$ is exactly the endomorphism component of the negligible tensor ideal generated by the boundary Jones–Wenzl projector $p_{\\ell-1}$. The $Q_n$ form the actual $A_{\\ell-1}$ path-space matrix tower of [[def-temperley-lieb-type-a-path-spaces-and-matrix-unit-tower]], with paths starting at $0$ and staying in $\\{0,\\ldots,k\\}$. Their simple modules are precisely the nonzero endpoint path spaces, and restriction branches with multiplicity one over adjacent predecessor vertices.\n\nReflection gives a finite-dimensional $C^*$-structure on $Q_n$ in which the normalized closure trace is faithful positive. The strand inclusions are injective unital $*$-maps and normalized right closure descends to the positive trace-preserving conditional expectation $\\bar E_n:Q_{n+1}\\to Q_n$ for $n\\ge1$. More explicitly, choose the normalized path matrix units $F_{p,q}$ whose prefix inclusions satisfy $F_{p,q}\\mapsto\\sum_c F_{pc,qc}$. If $pc,qc$ end at $c$, with predecessor endpoints $a,b$, then\n$$\\bar E_n(F_{pc,qc})=\\begin{cases}\\dfrac{[c+1]}{\\delta[a+1]}F_{p,q},&a=b,\\\\0,&a\\ne b.\\end{cases}$$\nHere the extensions and matrix units exist only for valid adjacent retained labels. The diagonal trace is $\\tau_n(F_{p,p})=\\delta^{-n}[a+1]$ when $p$ ends at $a$. These assertions hold at every finite rank, including the $\\ell=3$ boundary; no extra quotient/path identification is assumed.",
